# Title: Code Generation Rules
# Applies: Code Generation, Inline Edit

PYTHON
- Use `uv` for dependencies only (no direct pyproject edits).
- Enforce ruff (format + check), mypy type checking, pytest for tests.
- Document only when needed to explain “why”.
- Absolute imports only.

STRUCTURE & LIMITS
- Respect file/function/class limits from Global Standards.
- Split files approaching 300–500 lines by responsibility.
- Split functions approaching 30–50 lines or extract helpers.

PLANS FIRST
- Produce a concise implementation plan before coding.
- Note reuse opportunities found via `rg` searches.

PRE-COMPLETE CHECKLIST
- Precise type hints in all signatures.
- Domain exceptions for error paths.
- Logging at I/O boundaries and failures.
- Tests added/updated and passing.
- Code formatted and lint-clean.